          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "F"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Frame the geometry": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Frame the geometry"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cadrer la géométrie"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Create something": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Create something"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Créer quelque chose"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Open the Add menu, or click a button of the shelf under the 3D view, to make a node: a cube, a grid, a sphere. On an empty scene you can also start from an example.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Open the Add menu, or click a button of the shelf under the 3D view, to make a node: a cube, a grid, a sphere. On an empty scene you can also start from an example."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ouvrez le menu Ajouter, ou cliquez sur un bouton du bandeau sous la vue 3D, pour créer un nœud : un cube, une grille, une sphère. Sur une scène vide, vous pouvez aussi partir d’un exemple."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Import a model": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Import a model"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Importer un modèle"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Choose Add ▸ Import a 3D Model (⌘I), or drop a file on the window. Helix reads glTF, FBX, OBJ and more. The file itself is never changed.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Choose Add ▸ Import a 3D Model (⌘I), or drop a file on the window. Helix reads glTF, FBX, OBJ and more. The file itself is never changed."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Choisissez Ajouter ▸ Importer un modèle 3D (⌘I), ou déposez un fichier sur la fenêtre. Helix lit glTF, FBX, OBJ et d’autres formats. Le fichier lui-même n’est jamais modifié."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Move around the 3D view": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Move around the 3D view"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Se déplacer dans la vue 3D"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Nodes": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Nodes"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Nœuds"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A node is one step. Connect the output at the bottom of a node to the input at the top of the next. The flag marks the node the 3D view shows: double-click a node to show it. A node in error has a red outline and a warning triangle; select it to read why.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A node is one step. Connect the output at the bottom of a node to the input at the top of the next. The flag marks the node the 3D view shows: double-click a node to show it. A node in error has a red outline and a warning triangle; select it to read why."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Un nœud est une étape. Reliez la sortie, en bas d’un nœud, à l’entrée, en haut du suivant. Le drapeau marque le nœud que la vue 3D montre : double-cliquez sur un nœud pour l’afficher. Un nœud en erreur a un contour rouge et un triangle d’avertissement ; sélectionnez-le pour lire la cause."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The inspector": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The inspector"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "L’inspecteur"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Select a node to set its parameters on the right. Drag a slider or type a number. Right-click a parameter for expressions and keyframes.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Select a node to set its parameters on the right. Drag a slider or type a number. Right-click a parameter for expressions and keyframes."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sélectionnez un nœud pour régler ses paramètres, à droite. Faites glisser un curseur ou tapez un nombre. Un clic droit sur un paramètre donne accès aux expressions et aux images clés."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The timeline": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The timeline"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La chronologie"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Press the space bar to play. Right-click a parameter to key it: the diamonds on the ruler are its keys, and the line with a small triangle is the current frame.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Press the space bar to play. Right-click a parameter to key it: the diamonds on the ruler are its keys, and the line with a small triangle is the current frame."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Appuyez sur la barre d’espace pour lancer la lecture. Un clic droit sur un paramètre y pose une image clé : les losanges de la règle sont les images clés, et la ligne surmontée d’un petit triangle est l’image courante."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Save": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Save"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Enregistrer"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "⌘S saves the scene as a .kut file. A 3D file you open becomes a new scene that holds the model, and saving asks where to put it: the model itself is never written to.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "⌘S saves the scene as a .kut file. A 3D file you open becomes a new scene that holds the model, and saving asks where to put it: the model itself is never written to."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "⌘S enregistre la scène dans un fichier .kut. Un fichier 3D que vous ouvrez devient une nouvelle scène qui contient le modèle, et l’enregistrement demande où la ranger : le modèle lui-même n’est jamais modifié."
          }
        }
      }
    },
